WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.840
Film Courage: So let’s say there is a young
person in their car driving from Arizona to

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.350
Los Angeles, and you have a quick phone call
with them during this trip, what would be

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:07.500
your tough-love encouragement?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.780
Harvey Mason, Jr.: They are coming here to
work as a music producer, songwriter?

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.610
Film Courage: Music producer or it could be
anything within the industry but just the

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.560
general foundation [of what you would advise
them]?

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.910
Harvey Mason, Jr.: It would be a pretty long
conversation, but I would start with saying

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.250
if you’re going to come to Los Angeles,
be prepared for how competitive it is.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.470
There are so many people doing whatever it
is you want to do.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:32.080
There are thousands of them already here.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.900
There’s going to be another thousand of
them coming tomorrow and they are all probably

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.900
going to be better than you.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.370
So when you get here, be prepared for that.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.190
And figure out what you’re going to do to
get better than them.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:50.350
Come here with the mindset of I’m going
to have to really bust my butt to make it.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.590
Because a lot of people come here and think
“I’m so talented.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.830
My parents think I can sing.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.280
One of my teachers at my college said I’m
a great songwriter,” whatever…that’s

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:06.439
why everybody here is amazingly talented and
beautiful and handsome and whatever it is.

00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:10.180
That would be my first bit of advice and then
the other thing that I would say is be persistent.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.180
You can’t quit.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.180
You can’t give up.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.219
You have to prepare for the long haul.

00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:15.219
It’s not going to be quick.

00:01:15.219 --> 00:01:18.899
You’re not going to be able to come out
here and land an audition the first week you

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:22.859
get here or produce a song that goes on the
radio for years.

00:01:22.859 --> 00:01:24.530
It could take you years.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:25.530
Be prepared.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.530
Question for the Viewers: What advice would
you give to an artist who wants to move to

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:26.532
Los Angeles?

